    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261">

                <pb facs="0589" n="565" xml:id="pg565"/>

                <head>261. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Laos<anchor n="0" xml:id="d261-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-01-05T18:32:00-05:00">January 5, 1962,
                            6:32 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>594. Eyes Only for Ambassador.</p>
                <p>Have just seen President who strongly backs our insistence that Phoumi must not take initiative to break
                    cease-fire. Unless you are fully confident that measures already taken are
                    sufficient, please see Phoumi and tell him
                    that President has instructed you to inform him that resumption hostilities by
                    RLG under present circumstances would create situation in which RLG would have
                    no support either militarily or in terms of world or American opinion. President
                    does not believe possibilities peaceful solution Laotian question have been
                    fully exhausted and Phoumi should not
                    suppose, therefore, that US would join him in converting Laos into a
                    battleground with its devastating results to Laotian people.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Rusk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
